{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Sully appeals to me because a tense rescue with serious consequences fits the high-stakes stories I am interested in, as suggested by Taken 3 and 24.",
    "Goliath feels like a natural next choice because crime and legal suspense connect with my interest in the danger and tension of True Romance and 24."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Cafe Society's romantic comedy-drama focus does not fit my current desire for tension and action; being another screen story is not enough to interest me.",
    "I passed on the unnamed items because I could not establish what their stories were about, so those choices do not indicate that I dislike their actual content."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Cafe Society makes the connection to my viewing history feel too broad: I am looking for a particular kind of suspense, not just another film.",
    "My past interactions with unnamed items do not establish a shared preference that would make other unnamed items appealing to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The clearest connection among my identifiable recent choices is danger, urgency, and consequential conflict; that matters more to me right now than simply finding something else to watch.",
    "My interest can extend from action to a rescue story or legal suspense when the stakes remain compelling; it does not require the same exact premise."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "Sully and Goliath fit my interest in high-stakes tension, while Cafe Society misses that preference and the unnamed items leave their relevance uncertain."
}"}
